Avoid use-after-free of BeginFrameSource in ~CompositorFrameSinkSupport.

When CreateRootCompositorFrameSink replaces an existing entry in
root_sink_map_ (a misuse the upstream DCHECK at frame_sink_manager_impl.cc
line 217 doesn't catch in release builds), the old RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl
is destroyed by unique_ptr operator=. Its destructor body calls
UnregisterBeginFrameSource(), which usually clears support_'s borrowed
begin_frame_source_ via RecursivelyDetachBeginFrameSource ->
SetBeginFrameSource(nullptr). However the UnregisterBeginFrameSource
early-return path (no entry in frame_sink_source_map_) leaves that
borrowed pointer dangling.

The BFS unique_ptr members (synthetic_/external_begin_frame_source_) are
declared after support_ in RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl, so by reverse
member-destruction order they are freed first. Then ~CompositorFrameSinkSupport
runs SetNeedsBeginFrame(false) -> UpdateNeedsBeginFramesInternal ->
StopObservingBeginFrameSource, which dereferences the (non-null but stale)
begin_frame_source_ and crashes:

    Thread NN "VizCompositorThread" received signal SIGSEGV
    #0 viz::CompositorFrameSinkSupport::StopObservingBeginFrameSource
       at compositor_frame_sink_support.cc:1354 (begin_frame_source_->RemoveObserver(this))
    #3 ~CompositorFrameSinkSupport at line 141 (SetNeedsBeginFrame(false))
    #7 ~RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl at line 291 (member destruction)
    #14 FrameSinkManagerImpl::CreateRootCompositorFrameSink at line 240

Clear the borrowed pointer in ~RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl while the BFS
is still alive. SetBeginFrameSource(nullptr) is a no-op when
begin_frame_source_ is already null, so this is safe in the common path.

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc b/src/3rdparty/chromium/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
@@ -288,6 +288,12 @@ RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl::Create(
 RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl::~RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl() {
   support_->frame_sink_manager()->UnregisterBeginFrameSource(
       begin_frame_source());
+  // UnregisterBeginFrameSource() clears support_'s borrowed BFS pointer in
+  // the common path, but its early-return path (no entry in
+  // frame_sink_source_map_) leaves it dangling. The BFS members below are
+  // destroyed before support_; clear the pointer now so the upcoming
+  // ~CompositorFrameSinkSupport() does not dereference freed memory.
+  support_->SetBeginFrameSource(nullptr);
 }

